--- body ---
## Context

Migration [[0870]] rebuilt what was already extracted and extracted nothing new.
Measured 2026-09-29 on main (5382a1f5): 392 documents, 369 with a snapshot, 254 with lines (13,092
lines from 253 snapshots; `docs/jetp-requirements.md` DA2, which gives the
full count table), 115 snapshotted documents with zero lines, 23 with no
snapshot. Of the 13,092 lines, 10,452 are comparator records (CRS, IATI and
World Bank) in the 91 snapshots kept outside the document store. The join is
document, then `retrievals.sha256`, then `lines.sha256`: `snapshots.csv` has
no `document_id`.

The 115 by country: ZAF 49, SEN 28, VNM 25, IDN 13. By type: progress_update 24
(VNM 14, ZAF 9), project_page 27, data_portal 19, official_news 11,
annual_report 7, operator_report 8, project_list 8, implementation_plan 4,
investment_plan 3, approval_document 2, secondary_news 2. All 115 are active;
languages en 59, vi 20, fr 16, empty 20. Snapshot formats over the 115: HTML 66,
PDF 38, octet-stream 6, xlsx 2, JSON 2, JavaScript 2.

Dedup pass done at planning time (documents only, `docs/jetp-fusion.md` § 3): no
tier-1 group (same fingerprint) touches the 115; no `edition_of` row exists;
one title matches an already extracted document (to be checked by 1501). Tier 2
(normalised text) was not run: the snapshot bytes are not in a fresh worktree
(DVC), so 1501 runs it where the bytes are.

## What M2 is (normative text in the spec)

The accepted specification v1 (`docs/jetp-spec.md`, tag `jetp-spec-v1`)
governs; this tracker points at it and does not restate it. M2 is
`docs/jetp-requirements.md` § 2.2 (milestone M2), `docs/jetp-extraction.md`
§ 13 (the M2 slice) and `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 12 (the M2 and M3 slice).
In short: replay of the 254 extracted documents (comparator records by
ingestion run under the count control), idempotence, every one of the 392
documents ending with lines or a disposition, autonomous assisted reading
of the one-off documents (two blind local readers, a hosted arbiter,
calibration on held-out reference answers, nothing queued for the author),
transcription of the held scan, dated snapshots and restatements, budgets
and secrets, run reports and the run-output gate, and the off-site copy of
the document bytes with a restore test.

**Zotero (author decision 2026-10-01, interactive, D2).** The spec governs:
a one-way upload of every snapshot's bytes to the Zotero group, with its
SHA-256 in the item metadata, plus a test restore of one snapshot from each
off-disk copy (`docs/jetp-operation.md` § 9), is M2 and is carried by
[[1712]]. No job reads from Zotero at M2. The move of the document store
behind the registry interface ([[1510]], pilot [[1511]]) stays M4.

**M3a overlaps M2 (author decision 2026-10-01, interactive, D3).** The M3a
protocol declaration ([[1877]]) and the sealed known-item list ([[1878]])
may start now. M2 targets the register as frozen at 392 documents (369
with a snapshot): what M3a admits is extracted at M3b, not here.

## Pilot rule (author decision 2026-10-01, interactive)

Every long task (a full run, a batch, the replay, a transcription batch, a
selection run, a discovery campaign) first runs on a pilot sample,
stratified by country × format (language and statement shape where the
task reads text), with its size stated. A quality check on the pilot
passes, and its findings are recorded on the task's ticket, before the task
is scaled up. The checker is not the author: a cross-model or second-vendor
check, with only its residue going to the author. Each long-task child
carries an exit criterion to that effect.

## Phases

M2 is cut along three dimensions:

- **Lane.** The deterministic lane (parsers, ingestion runs, the replay,
  with an oracle that already exists) against the reading lane (two LLM
  readers, the arbiter, calibration, budgets). The deterministic lane runs
  first: it needs no LLM and no paid call.
- **Format.** Adapters per format (text-layer PDF, HTML, spreadsheet, JSON;
  a scan needs transcription), each with its own text layer.
- **Country and language** are the strata of every pilot sample and
  calibration, not separate tickets; a country gets its own ticket only when
  it is a separate sign-off unit.

| Phase | What | Children | Lane |
|---|---|---|---|
| M2.0 | Schema and core: the M2 storage targets, the pipeline core, the run report, run-output gate and agent permissions | [[1870]], [[1506]], [[1875]] | both |
| M2.1 | Deterministic replay, no LLM: the 254 extracted documents, the comparator records by ingestion run under the count control | [[1507]] | deterministic |
| M2.2 | Format adapters | [[1508]] | both |
| M2.3 | Reading: assisted reading protocol, reader selection and calibration, budgets and guards, transcription of the held scan | [[1509]], [[1873]], [[1874]], [[1876]] | reading |
| M2.4 | The run over the 115: dedup, the four waves, dispositions | [[1501]], [[1502]], [[1503]], [[1504]], [[1505]] | both |
| M2.x | Off-site copy of the document bytes and restore test; may run in any phase | [[1712]] | — |

The phase order is the dependency order recorded in the children's
`Blocked-by`; a phase may start as soon as its own blockers close.
Departures from the suggested order, and why: transcription ([[1876]]) sits
in M2.3, not M2.2, because extraction § 6.4 reads a scan with two hosted
vision readers and the arbiter under the § 6.3 protocol, so only its
recogniser text layer is an adapter; the run report and gate ([[1875]]) sit
in M2.0 because the M2.1 replay is already a run.

## Pipeline stages

1. Registry and dedup gate ([[1501]]). 2. Bytes by `sha256`, behind a registry
interface. 3. Text layer, cached by hash and adapter version. 4. Extractor:
a per-series parser, an ingestion run, assisted reading, or transcription
(`docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 6). 5. Writer: append-only lines,
`line-field-specs`, the journals of [[1870]] (runs, readings, dispositions,
restatements). 6. Validator (`make jetp-ledger-check`) and the run-output
gate of [[1875]]. Build from cases: the first parser is the VNM progress
updates; generalise after two or three cases, not before.

## Relation to other work

- M1b ([[0833]]) was accepted on 2026-10-01 ([[0725]]).
- The registry interface of 1506 is the seam for the M4 document store
  ([[1510]], [[1511]]), as [[1140]] and [[1184]] already require of
  acquisition; the text layer of 1508 takes up [[1512]].
- Document relations (`same_as`, `edition_of`, `translation_of`): for M2 the
  home is the ledger, because 1501 needs them before any Zotero item exists.
  1510 decision 2 places editions and translations in Zotero as linked
  items; at M4 the ledger rows become the source of that migration.
- [[0920]] finishes the 55 pending links of 0874 and overlaps only on the
  documents it acquires. M2 may retry, on the first two rungs of the access
  ladder, the retrieval of registered documents without a snapshot
  (`docs/jetp-collection.md` § 11, "M2 before the campaign").
- The storage targets of M3a and M3b are [[1871]] and [[1872]] (tracker
  [[1702]]), not M2.

## Invariants

- Lines of the 254 extracted documents are byte-identical before and after.
- Lines of an earlier snapshot are never edited by a later snapshot's run.
- `make jetp-ledger-check` passes at every child.
- A `line_id` is appended, never renumbered; ordinals continue across
  snapshots (`docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 9).
- Duplicates are resolved before extraction; a revoked duplicate judgement
  re-enables extraction of the document it had folded (`docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 2).
- No item of a run is queued for the author (`docs/jetp-operation.md` § 4).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] M2.0 closed: [[1870]] (M2 schema slice of [[1702]]), [[1506]], [[1875]]
- [ ] M2.1 closed: [[1507]]; the replay of the 254 extracted documents passes, comparator records included under the count control
- [ ] M2.2 closed: [[1508]]
- [ ] M2.3 closed: [[1509]], [[1873]], [[1874]], [[1876]]
- [ ] M2.4 closed: [[1501]], [[1502]], [[1503]], [[1504]], [[1505]]
- [ ] [[1712]] closed: every snapshot uploaded one way to the Zotero group, and one snapshot restored from each off-disk copy and checked by hash
- [ ] All 392 documents have lines or a recorded disposition with the reason; the deferred ones are named by country and type
- [ ] Each extractor was red-tested against a defect it must reject, and each long task passed its pilot check
- [ ] A second dated snapshot runs through the pipeline and appends dated lines without touching earlier ones, on the fixture and held page of `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 13 ([[1506]])
- [ ] Author acceptance of M2 after an integration review, recorded in [[0725]]
